# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Root .gitignore for the Alrhalla monorepo.
#
# backend/, rhalla_agent/ and ExchangeSystem/ each keep their own
# .gitignore and git still honours them. What is here is either
# repo-wide, or a deliberate second line of defence around the
# credential files — those must never reach GitHub even if a
# sub-.gitignore is edited later.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# --- Credentials: never commit, at any depth ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.env.bak
RhallaConfig.ini
!RhallaConfig.ini.template
key.properties
!key.properties.template
*.jks
*.keystore
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
auth.json

# --- OS / editor noise ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp

# --- Python caches (from .claude/skills scripts) ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# --- Dependency + build output (backstop; sub-ignores cover these too) ---
node_modules/
vendor/
/backend/env
/backend/L
